    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "State the axis in which\n$$x(x-1)+y(y-1)=1$$\nis reflected to give $x(x+1)+y(y-1)=1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y$-axis.",
      "worked": "Replace $x$ by $-x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(-x)(-x-1)+y(y-1)&=1\\\\x(x+1)+y(y-1)&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nThe reflection is in the $y$-axis.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
